<article class="env-lemma" id="00PM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PM">Lemma <span data-tag="00PM">10.122.5</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a finite type ring map. Then $R \to S$ is quasi-finite if and only if for all primes $\mathfrak p \subset R$ the ring $S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ is finite over $\kappa (\mathfrak p)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from the more general Lemma <a href="/tag/0H8X" data-tag="0H8X">10.122.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>